  "articleBody": "Installing a new lever-style kitchen faucet can really upgrade your kitchen, but it's easy to make a few common mistakes that can lead to headaches down the line. First off, never skip flushing your lines before regular use. Debris can get knocked loose during installation and clog your new faucet right away. Another big one is overtightening supply connections; you can actually damage the components, leading to leaks you'll have to fix later. On the flip side, not tightening them enough means leaks too! It's a Goldilocks situation. Also, make sure you're testing all connections, including the aerator and spray, for leaks before you call it done. It's much easier to catch a small drip now than to deal with water damage later. Lastly, always confirm your new faucet's hole count and spacing matches your sink. Getting that wrong means a return trip to the store or a more complex installation. If you're ever unsure, especially with older plumbing or if you need to reconfigure existing lines, don't hesitate to reach out to a local expert like HH Remodeling LLC. We're happy to help homeowners in Aurora and the greater Denver area get it right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}